  "checks": [
    "All 13 relocated definitions preserve effective matching, criticality, scope and dependency sets after ID remapping.",
    "Ten inert PE controls cover changed call targets, changed encoded variable, absent profiler gate, absent assembly load, absent decompressor, file-backed versus memory-only code, and admin versus asInvoker manifests.",
    "Six pre-existing binary controls preserve their complete mapped finding sets."
  ],
  "unresolved_hostile_coverage": "No generic hostile trait can be justified from the commercial wrapper alone. The recovered managed image virtualizes methods and encrypts its strings; cleave does not expose the VM-decoded persistence, Defender-exclusion, UAC-bypass or remote-tasking operations. The x64 aPLib recovery exposes the WinLicense protector but leaves application code protected. Analysis-tool termination attempts and remote-memory writes are documented in the sandbox, but their native decoder output is not available to YAML matchers. These remain detection gaps, not a completed hostile-coverage goal.",
  "classifier_disagreement": "All three retain level=-1 and confidence=0 despite probabilities above 0.90. Reported engine warning: model feature-spec version 18 versus expected 21. No inaccurate traits or duplicate hostile composites were introduced to alter the calibrated outcome.",
